gnyan po gsang ba|(Text) The twenty-eighth Yarlung king, Lhatotori Nyentsen (Lha-tho-tho-ri gNyan-btsan) (b. 173 CE) received [a basket of] Buddhist scriptures from India, written in Sanskrit, called "the Tough Mystery". Quest. to Alex, would “Großes Mysterium” „great mystery“ be fine as well? NO. THE TIBETAN TERM, WHICH I TRANSLATED AS “TOUGH” IN “TOUGH MYSTERY” MEANS FEROCIOUS, FORCEFUL, SO THAT IMPLIES QUITE DIFFICULT TO UNRAVEL. Monika: we decided therfore in German for "schwierig" ("difficult"), which is also a translation of "tough".
