gsang sngags kyi tshul khrims kyi rnam bshad dngos grub kyi snye ma|(Text) Author: Tsongkhapa (tsong kha pa blo bzang grags pa). Question: In the heading of the article "An Explanation of Secret Mantra Ethical Discipline: A Cluster of Fruit of Actual Attainments" the collocation "Ethical Discipline" is translated only as "Ethic". And in the heading "An Explanation of Bodhisattvas' Ethical Discipline: The Main Path to Enlightenment" this collocation is translated as "Ethical Discipline". Should we change the translation of the first heading? ALEX: IT IS THE NAME OF A TEXT, NOT AN ARTICLE. IN BOTH TEXT TITLES IT SHOULD BE ETHICAL DISCIPLINE. Question: [2] Can we say "collection of fruits"? If no, can we say "Cluster of Fruits" - in plural? Does it mean raceme - like it is on a tree? ALEX: USE CLUSTER OF FRUITS. YES IT IS LIKE A RACEME, OR WHEAT ON A STALK, OR BERRIES ON A BUSH, OR GRAPES.
