mdo sde pa|A Hinayana school of Indian Buddhism that asserts the true existence of both reflexive awareness and external phenomena; a subdivision of the Sarvastivada school of Hinayana. One of the four Indian Buddhist tenet systems studied by all traditions of Tibetan Buddhism.
mdo sde rgyan|(Text) Author: Maitreya (byams pa). ALEX: The text is an explanation of the main points of the Mahayana sutras and is one of the first Indian commentaries on Mahayana. So it is a beautiful elaborate piece of jewelry which is presented by its author as something to put on the sutras to adorn them and make them easier to understand. Thus it is a Filigree for the Mahayana Sutras, like a gift that the author is giving to the sutras Question: Could we say "Ornament for the Mahayana Sutras". In Russian "filigree" is quite rare word. For instance, i didn't know the meaning of the word "filigree" until i faced it in someone's translation of your articles. ALEX: IN ENGLISH, ORNAMENT SOUNDS PRETTY STRANGE, ALTHOUGH EVERYONE USES IT FOR RGYAN IN TITLES. RGYAN MEANS IS A VERY COMPLEX INTERTWINED ELABORATE PIECE OF JEWELRY. IF FILIGREE IS A WORD THAT NO ONE WOULD KNOW IN RUSSIAN, AND IF ORNAMENT DOESN;T SOUND LIKE A PIECE OF SCULPTURE DECORATING THE TOP OF THE OUTSIDE WALL OF A GREEK TEMPLE, THEN OK. Skt: Full: Short: Mahayanasutralamkara.
mdo sde sa bcu pa|(Text) Skt: Full: Short: Dashabhumika Sutra.
mdo sde spyod pa'i dbu ma rang rgyud pa|(Tradition)
mdo sde spyod pa'i dbu ma rang rgyud pa|According to Gelug, a subdivision of the Svatantrika Madhyamaka tenet system that does not assert reflexive awareness, but does assert external phenomena as having existence established by their individual defining characteristic marks.
