mi rtag sgom tshul gyi bslab bya tshigs su bcad pa bcas|(Text) Author: Gungthang Rinpoche (gung thang tshang dkon mchog bstan pa'i sgron me).
mi shes sgrib|Mental blocks that come from not knowing the Dharma in general or specifically not knowing about the emotional and cognitive obscurations. These mental blocks prevent the attainment of liberation and enlightenment.
mi slob lam|The level of mind of shravaka arhats, pratyekabuddha arhats, and Buddhas, with which they have attained their respective purified states (bodhi) of liberation or enlightenment, and which requires no further training in order to attain that purified state. Other translators sometimes render this term as "path of no learning."
mi srid pa|A phenomenon that cannot be validly known now. It may be either an existent phenomenon (such as a no-longer happening or a not-yet-happening one) or a nonexistent phenomenon.
mig gi spyod yul du 'gyur ba'i gzugs|Equivalent to sights. See: sights.
ming|A combination of sounds that are assigned a meaning.
ming 'dogs pa|To impute (project, superimpose), with conceptual cognition, an audio category (such as the word or name "table") or a meaning/object category (such as a "table" as an individual object) onto a basis (such as four legs and a flat board on top of them). Also translated as "imputation."
ming chen|(Person) Skt: Mahanama.
ming dang gzugs kyi yan lag|The fourth of the twelve links of dependent arising. The four mental aggregates -- consciousness, feeling a level of happiness, distinguishing, and other affecting variables -- some of which are merely potentials -- together with the aggregate of forms of physical phenomena during a rebirth on the plane of sensory desires or the plane of ethereal forms, or without this aggregate during a rebirth on the plane of formless beings, during the period of time in the development of a foetus from the moment of conception up until the moment just before the cognitive faculties of seeing, hearing, and so on are differentiated.
mkha' 'gro ma rdo rje gur shes bya ba'i rgyud kyi rgyal po chen po'i brtag pa|(Text) Skt: Full: Ḍākinī-vajra-pañjara­mahātantra-rājā-kalpa-nāma Short:.
