sku zhang mkhyen rab chos rje|(Person)
skur 'debs|A conceptual denial of something that is true or is present.
skyab 'gro tsam pa ba|Synonymous with "causal taking of safe direction."
skyabs|A direction that one puts in one's life that will protect one from true suffering and its true causes, and, when one reaches the goal of this direction, allows one to avoid true suffering and its true causes forever. Some translators render this as "refuge."
skyabs 'gro|To put a direction in one's life, which, when one goes in it, protects one from true suffering and its true causes and which, when one reaches its endpoint, allows one to avoid true suffering and its true causes forever. Some translators render this as "take refuge," but it has no connotation of merely opening up and passively receiving protection.
skyabs 'gro bdun cu pa|(Text) Author: Chandrakirti. Skt: with Diacritics: Full: Triśaraṇa-saptati Short:.
skyabs 'gro khyad par ba|Synonym for "resultant taking of safe direction."
