skyabs yul|A general term for the Buddha, Dharma, and Sangha.
skye ba|(1) The moment when the consciousness of a bardo being enters its next rebirth. In the case of rebirth as a human or an animal, the moment in which it enters the sperm and egg of its next parents. (2) See: concept.
skye ba'i yan lag|The eleventh of the twelve links of dependent arising, equivalent to the first moment of the link of nameable mental faculties with or without gross form. The moment when the consciousness of a bardo being enters its next rebirth. In the case of rebirth as a human or an animal, the moment in which it enters the sperm and egg of its next parents.
skye bo bsu bde|(Person)
skye dgu'i bdag mo|(Person)
skye dgu'i bdag mo chen mo|(Person) Skt: Mahaprajapati.
skye mched|The focal conditions and dominating conditions that give rise to the six types of cognition -- namely, the cognitive objects and cognitive sensors of each of the six cognitive faculties. In the case of the five sensory faculties, the objects and sensors are forms of physical phenomena, such as sights and photosensitive cells. In the case of the mental faculty, the objects may be any validly knowable phenomenon, while the sensors are the immediately preceding moments of mental cognition. Usually counted as the twelve stimulators of cognition, but in the list of the twelve links of dependent arising, referred to as the six stimulators of cognition, in which case the two cognitive stimulators of each cognitive faculty are counted as one.
skye mched bcu gnyis|The twelve classes of nonstatic phenomena that serve as focal and dominating conditions for the six types of cognition -- namely, (1) sights, (2) eye sensors, (3) sounds, (4) ear sensors, (5) smells, (6) nose sensors, (7) tastes, (8) tongue sensors, (9) physical sensations, (10) body sensors, (11) (all) phenomena, and (12) mind sensors.
skye mched kyi yan lag|The fifth of the twelve links of dependent arising. The stimulators of cognition during the period of time in the development of a fetus from when the six different stimulators of cognition are differentiated up until but just before the aggregate of distinguishing is differentiated.
skye srid|The period of time in the mental continuum of an individual limited being during which they experience conception. It lasts only one moment. Some translators render the term as "birth existence."
skyer sgang lugs kyi rta mgrin gsang sgrub kyi sgrub thabs rgyas pa rta mchog rol pa'i zhal lung|(Text)
skyes bu|See: person
skyes bu byed pa'i 'bras bu|A result that arises as the direct result of the effort of a limited being, but which does not ripen from karma.
skyes bu gsum gyi lam rim rgyas pa khrid su sbyar ba|(Text) Author: Sangwayjin (gsang ba'i byin).
skyes bu gsum gyi nyams su blang ba'i byang chub lam gyi rim pa|(Text) Author: Tsongkhapa.
skyes pa'i rabs|Accounts of the difficult ascetic practices that Buddha performed in his previous lives while engaging in the conduct of the bodhisattvas. One of the twelve scriptural categories.
